Prefixes are element-indexed!

- Current prefix contains `arr[0, r]`
- Earlier prefix includes `arr[0, l]`
- Subarray is `arr[l + 1, r]` (length `r - l`)

```c
freq[0] = 1;

long prefix = 0;
long count = 0;

for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    prefix += arr[i];

    int rem = prefix % K;
    if (rem < 0) rem += K;  // normalize negative modulo!

    count += freq[rem];
    freq[rem]++;
}

return count;
```

Idiom: A subarray sum is divisible by `K` when its two boundary prefix sums have the same remainder modulo `K`. Every earlier occurrence of the current remainder identifies one qualifying subarray.

```c
// Stores first occurrence of each prefix sum
unordered_map<long, int> first;

first[0] = -1;

long prefix = 0;
int longest = 0;

for (int r = 0; r < n; r++) {
  prefix += arr[r];

  if (first.contains(prefix - K)) {
    int l = first[prefix - K];
    int len = r - l;
    if (len > longest) longest = len;
  }

  // Record this prefix if not seen yet
  if (!first.contains(prefix)) first[prefix] = r;

}

return longest;
```
